  "function": {
    "uniprot_function": "Receptor for Wnt proteins. Functions in the canonical Wnt/beta-catenin signaling pathway. The canonical Wnt/beta-catenin signaling pathway leads to the activation of disheveled proteins, inhibition of GSK-3 kinase, nuclear accumulation of beta-catenin and activation of Wnt target genes. Activated by WNT3A, WNT3, WNT1 and to a lesser extent WNT2, but apparently not by WNT4, WNT5A, WNT5B, WNT6, WNT7A or WNT7B. Functions in adult hippocampal neurogenesis.",
    "catalytic_activity": "Not applicable - functions as a receptor, not an enzyme",
    "subcellular_location": ["Plasma membrane"],
    "tissue_specificity": "Expressed in multiple tissues with low tissue specificity. Detected in brain, heart, kidney, liver, lung, pancreas, prostate, ovary, fetal heart, and fetal kidney. Overexpressed in ovary, cerebral cortex, seminal vesicle, placenta, and fetal heart.",
