    "pathway_role_summary": "FZD1 functions as a seven-transmembrane receptor for WNT ligands in the canonical Wnt/beta-catenin signaling pathway. Upon WNT3A binding to the CRD domain, FZD1 forms a ternary complex with LRP5/6 co-receptors, leading to recruitment and activation of cytoplasmic Dishevelled (DVL) proteins through the C-terminal PDZ-binding motif. DVL recruitment triggers disassembly of the beta-catenin destruction complex, allowing beta-catenin nuclear translocation and TCF/LEF-mediated transcription. FZD1 can also signal through beta-catenin-independent (non-canonical) pathways including planar cell polarity (PCP) pathway. The receptor couples to heterotrimeric G proteins (particularly Gq) to activate downstream signaling cascades."
  },
